# Jak 3: Jak's hands on a city vehicle's handlebars or wheel (LIST-0.1.9 items 6 and 7; a tester: "jak's hands dont
# grab handdle bars of bike style zoomers", "hover car hand holds close enough but adjustments could improve them").
# Run with JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=ctysluma-start JAKVR_TEST_WARP=h-bike-a (or h-bike-b, h-bike-c; h-car-a, h-car-b,
# h-car-c for the cars) JAKVR_TEST_RIDE=1 QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000 JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1: a new game into play (as
# jak3_shadow_walk.sim), the continue, Jak put beside the nearest of that type and on it (frame 10000). Then pictures:
# seated with the hands free, both grips squeezed (the hands on the game's handles), from the right side and the left
# with the view let free, turned, let go. Expect "[vr-test] ride: Jak is on it", "[vr-pad] the wheel held by ..." and
# his hands closed on the bars or the wheel the game draws, seen from the eyes and from the sides.
# A (Cross) every 200 frames from 3100 to 4500 closes the new game's save notice (it hid the view in sim pg; only A, as
# Triangle would get Jak off a vehicle).
# 0.1.9 (sim s11 vh3b on build 129): the free view moves the eyes but does not turn them, so "held-above" showed only the
# road; now the head looks 70 degrees down while the grips are held ("vh-held-down"): his hands on the bars, under the
# eyes on Jak 3's bikes (the game's handles 37 cm under them, 3 cm ahead).
